summary:
  A cancel goes back to looking for a pid and nothing else: it leaves no
  mark for a measurement that is still getting ready.

history:
  The calibration is one shell command that asks every speaker for its
  level, parks it at 55 % and only then starts calibrate.py and writes the
  pid down. Driven on 2026-11-11 with the engine's own command, stand-ins
  for pactl and python, and the first level query held back: at Cancel
  there was no pid file, nothing was signalled, and when the query came
  back the shell parked all three speakers and started the measurement
  that had been called off. Once the pid was written the same cancel
  worked. The mark is the only word that reaches a shell in that state.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CalibLogic.js

find:
      return (t === "" ? "" : " [ -n \"$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\" ] && printf '%s' '" + t + "' > " + markFile + ";")

replace:
      return ("")

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_calibrate_cancel.py::test_cancel_during_the_first_query_parks_nothing_and_starts_nothing.
  Line-neutral.
